From: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: fix multicast queue AC table
 access

The multicast admission-control table has one 16-byte entry per
multicast queue (44 entries at 0x84a000), indexed from the first
multicast queue, as the vendor SSDK does with obj_id - UCAST_QUEUE_ID_MAX
and as its shipped qca-ssdk.ko does with a subtraction of 256. The driver
indexes it with the absolute queue ID (256 to 299), which lands 0x1000
past the table, so the multicast thresholds were never written. It also
transfers five words per entry while the entry holds three and the
stride is four, so each write spilled into the next entry.

Index the table relative to the first multicast queue and transfer the
three words the entry has. The driver only touches words 0 and 2.

Signed-off-by: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_config.c
@@ -1716,7 +1716,7 @@
 {
 	const struct ppe_qm_queue_config *queue_cfg;
 	int ret, i, queue_id, queue_cfg_count;
-	u32 reg, multicast_queue_cfg[5];
+	u32 reg, multicast_queue_cfg[3];
 	u32 unicast_queue_cfg[4];
 	u32 group_cfg[3];
 	int group_limit;
@@ -1781,8 +1781,12 @@
 				if (ret)
 					goto qm_config_fail;
 			} else {
+				/* The multicast table is indexed relative to the
+				 * first multicast queue.
+				 */
 				reg = PPE_AC_MULTICAST_QUEUE_CFG_TBL_ADDR +
-				      PPE_AC_MULTICAST_QUEUE_CFG_TBL_INC * queue_id;
+				      PPE_AC_MULTICAST_QUEUE_CFG_TBL_INC *
+				      (queue_id - PPE_AC_UNICAST_QUEUE_CFG_TBL_ENTRIES);
 
 				ret = regmap_bulk_read(ppe_dev->regmap, reg,
 						       multicast_queue_cfg,
